1999</year><fpage>143</fpage><lpage>151</lpage><article-title>Body image perception in relation to recent weight changes and strategies for weight loss in a nationally representative sample in the European Union</article-title><source>Public Health Nutr</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10933634</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sandman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Simantov</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>An</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><publisher-loc>New York (NY)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>The Commonwealth Fund</publisher-name><source>Out of touch: American men and the health care system. Commonwealth Fund Men's and Women's Health Survey findings</source></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Galuska</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Will</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Serdula</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Ford</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name></person-group><volume>282</volume><issue>16</issue><year>1999</year><fpage>1576</fpage><lpage>1578</lpage><article-title>Are health care professionals advising obese patients to lose weight?</article-title><source>JAMA</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10546698</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B33"><label>33</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simkin-Silverman</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name><name><surname>Gleason</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name><name><surname>Weissfeld</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Buhari</surname><given-names>A</given-